### TopUp Wallet — "Try It" full flow, top to bottom.
### Run each request in order with the REST Client extension (VS Code) or Rider.
### The stack must be up:  docker compose up -d
### Click "Send Request" above each request. Later requests reuse the token +
### ids from earlier responses automatically (request variables), so run in order.

@auth   = http://localhost:5003
@wallet = http://localhost:5001
@topup  = http://localhost:5002
@json   = application/json

### ── 0. Health (open, no token) ──
GET {{wallet}}/health

### ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### 1. LOG IN  → returns accessToken + refreshToken (any non-empty creds)
# @name login
POST {{auth}}/auth/login
Content-Type: {{json}}

{ "username": "demo", "password": "any" }

###
@token = {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### 2a. Create an account WITHOUT a token → 401 Unauthorized (auth works)
POST {{wallet}}/accounts
Content-Type: {{json}}

{ "ownerName": "No Auth", "currency": "USD", "opening": 0 }

### ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### 2b. Create an account WITH the token → 201, balance 0, returns id
# @name createAccount
POST {{wallet}}/accounts
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: {{json}}

{ "ownerName": "Demo", "currency": "USD", "opening": 0 }

###
@accountId = {{createAccount.response.body.$.id}}

### ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### 3. FUND THE WALLET (money IN via the payment gateway)
### 3a. Create a $100 deposit (card token "tok_ok"). Returns a PENDING deposit.
###     Balance is NOT credited yet — money lands only on the signed webhook.
# @name createDeposit
POST {{wallet}}/accounts/{{accountId}}/deposits
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: {{json}}

{ "paymentToken": "tok_ok", "amount": 100 }

###
@depositId = {{createDeposit.response.body.$.depositId}}

### 3b. Check balance now → still 0 (webhook hasn't arrived)
GET {{wallet}}/accounts/{{accountId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 3c. Get a correctly-SIGNED webhook payload for this deposit (demo helper)
# @name webhookPayload
POST {{wallet}}/accounts/{{accountId}}/deposits/{{depositId}}/webhook-payload
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
@webhookBody = {{webhookPayload.response.body.$.body}}
@webhookSig  = {{webhookPayload.response.body.$.signature}}

### 3d. POST the webhook with a VALID signature → wallet credited. Balance → 100.
POST {{wallet}}/webhooks/payment
X-Signature: {{webhookSig}}
Content-Type: {{json}}

{{webhookBody}}

### 3e. Balance now → 100
GET {{wallet}}/accounts/{{accountId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 3f. REPLAY the same webhook (PSPs retry) → idempotent, balance STILL 100
POST {{wallet}}/webhooks/payment
X-Signature: {{webhookSig}}
Content-Type: {{json}}

{{webhookBody}}

### 3g. FORGED webhook (bad signature) → 401, no credit
POST {{wallet}}/webhooks/payment
X-Signature: deadbeef-not-a-real-signature
Content-Type: {{json}}

{{webhookBody}}

### ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### 4. TOP UP A PHONE (money OUT via the saga)
### 4a. Happy path: $5 → wallet debited, operator charged OK. Balance → 95.
###     Returns 202 Accepted + topUpId + fee (the saga runs async).
POST {{topup}}/topups
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: {{json}}

{ "accountId": "{{accountId}}", "phoneNumber": "+8801711000000", "amount": 5, "idempotencyKey": "demo-ok-1" }

### 4b. Decline path: $5.13 (cents .13 → operator declines) → debited then
###     AUTO-REFUNDED by the saga's compensation. Balance back to 95.
POST {{topup}}/topups
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: {{json}}

{ "accountId": "{{accountId}}", "phoneNumber": "+8801711000000", "amount": 5.13, "idempotencyKey": "demo-fail-1" }

### (wait ~2-3 seconds for the async saga to settle, then inspect below)

### ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### 5. INSPECT
### 5a. Balance → 95  (100 funded, −5 happy top-up, 5.13 debited+refunded nets 0)
GET {{wallet}}/accounts/{{accountId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 5b. SQL ledger — immutable, append-only. See debit 5, then debit 5.13, then
###     a refund credit 5.13 (the compensation — an opposite entry, not a rollback).
GET {{wallet}}/accounts/{{accountId}}/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 5c. Mongo audit trail (append-only event log), paginated
GET {{wallet}}/accounts/{{accountId}}/audit?page=1&pageSize=50
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### 6. OWNERSHIP / IDOR — a DIFFERENT user cannot touch this account
# @name loginOther
POST {{auth}}/auth/login
Content-Type: {{json}}

{ "username": "mallory", "password": "any" }

###
@otherToken = {{loginOther.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### 6a. Another user reads Demo's account → 403 Forbidden (ownership check)
GET {{wallet}}/accounts/{{accountId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{otherToken}}

### 6b. Another user debits Demo's account → 403 Forbidden
POST {{wallet}}/accounts/{{accountId}}/debit
Authorization: Bearer {{otherToken}}
Content-Type: {{json}}

{ "amount": 10, "idempotencyKey": "mallory-steal" }

### ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### 7. REFRESH — exchange the refresh token for a new access + refresh pair
@refreshToken = {{login.response.body.$.refreshToken}}

POST {{auth}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: {{json}}

{ "refreshToken": "{{refreshToken}}" }
